cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PlannerDNA: Learning and Blind-Testing Personal Pairwise Preference Models in a Local-First 3D Urban-Design Sandbox"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alpha
    alias: sandaru01-IH
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/sandaru01-IH/PlannerDNA"
abstract: >-
  PlannerDNA is a local-first Unity 6 urban-design sandbox in which a participant designs two
  alternative plans for a procedurally generated neighbourhood and explicitly chooses between them.
  A FastAPI and SQLite backend re-verifies every design, fits an interpretable pairwise logistic
  (Bradley-Terry) model on five baseline-relative features with bootstrap uncertainty and
  leave-one-scenario-out diagnostics, and evaluates the frozen model with a pre-registered,
  blinded protocol using SHA-256 sealed predictions on unseen cities.
keywords:
  - urban planning
  - preference learning
  - pairwise comparison
  - Bradley-Terry model
  - blinded evaluation
  - Unity
  - FastAPI
  - serious games
